{# Everything get_student_records says back to the model.

   Same split as tools/knowledge_result.j2: backend/tools/records.py DECIDES which
   outcome occurred, this file renders it. Each branch is paid only on the turns where
   its condition is real, so the system prompt stays silent about all of it.

   The rule running through every failure branch: a records answer is about a real
   child, and a plausible invention is worse than an admission. The wording below
   closes the gap the model would otherwise fill — "temporarily unavailable" and "no
   grades recorded" are different sentences and must never be swapped.

   Field access is via .get() throughout. The environment uses StrictUndefined, and a
   facade that adds or drops an optional field should degrade to a blank in one line,
   never raise mid-turn and take the whole answer down. `any_in_progress` and
   `any_excused` arrive precomputed for the same reason the outcome does: deciding
   them is the tool's job, and doing it in Jinja means a filter chain that explodes on
   the first row missing a key.

   Long sentence lines are deliberate; see the note in knowledge_result.j2.

   Whitespace: trim_blocks is on, so the newline after every {% %} tag is swallowed. #}
{% if outcome == "call_limit" %}
TOOL_CALL_LIMIT_REACHED: get_student_records has been called the maximum number of times this turn. Answer from what it already returned; do not call it again.
{% elif outcome == "not_a_parent" %}
NOT_A_PARENT_SESSION: this conversation is not signed in as a parent, so no student records can be looked up. Tell the user that viewing a student's records requires signing in as their registered parent or guardian, and offer to help with general school information instead. Do not ask them to type a student name, ID or date of birth — those cannot authorise anything and collecting them here is pointless.
{% elif outcome == "not_authorized" %}
NOT_AUTHORIZED: the school records system did not accept this session's identity — most likely the sign-in has expired. Tell the user to sign in again and retry. Do NOT say the student has no records, and do not answer from anything earlier in the conversation.
{% elif outcome == "unavailable" %}
RECORDS_UNAVAILABLE: the school records system could not be reached. Tell the user briefly that records are temporarily unavailable and to try again shortly. Do NOT state, estimate or infer any grade, mark, average or attendance figure — not from earlier in this conversation, not from the knowledge base, and not from your own reasoning. An invented figure about a real child is the worst possible outcome here.
{% elif outcome == "no_students" %}
NO_STUDENTS_LINKED: this parent's account is not linked to any student the school will release records for. Tell them their account has no student linked to it yet and that the school office can arrange this. Do not speculate about why, and do not name any student.
{% elif outcome == "which_student" %}
NEEDS_STUDENT_CHOICE: more than one child is linked to this parent, and it is not clear which one they mean.
{% if options %}
Children: {{ options | join("; ") }}
{% endif %}
Ask the parent which child they are asking about. Do not pick one, and do not show any figures until they answer.
{% elif outcome == "which_subject" %}
NEEDS_SUBJECT_CHOICE: the subject was not clear from the question.
{% if options %}
Subjects recorded this term: {{ options | join("; ") }}
{% endif %}
Ask which subject they mean. Do not guess.
{% elif outcome == "no_records" %}
NO_RECORDS: the school records system has nothing recorded for this request. Tell the user plainly that nothing is recorded yet for that. This means the record is absent, NOT that the student scored zero or was absent — do not describe it as a poor result.
{% elif outcome == "grades" %}
STUDENT_GRADES for {{ student_label }}{% if term_label %} — {{ term_label }}{% endif %}{% if academic_year_label %} ({{ academic_year_label }}){% endif %}:
{% if courses %}
{% for course in courses %}
- {{ course.get('subject_name_ar') or course.get('subject_name_en') }}: {% if course.get('computed_percentage') is not none %}{{ course.get('computed_percentage') }}%{% if course.get('letter_grade') %} ({{ course.get('letter_grade') }}){% endif %}{% else %}no grade recorded yet{% endif %}{% if course.get('excused_count') %} — {{ course.get('excused_count') }} excused{% endif %}{% if course.get('missing_count') %} — {{ course.get('missing_count') }} not submitted{% endif %}{% if not course.get('is_complete') %} — still in progress{% endif %}

{% endfor %}

Report these figures as they stand. Do not recalculate, average across subjects, or convert to a different scale — the school's own weighting has already been applied and a second calculation will disagree with the report card.
{% if any_in_progress %}
Some subjects are marked still in progress: their figure is the result so far, not a final grade. Say so rather than presenting it as settled.
{% endif %}
{% if any_excused %}
"Excused" means the school exempted that work; it is not counted against the student and is not a zero. If the parent asks about it, say so — do not describe excused work as missed or as a bad mark.
{% endif %}
{% else %}
No subjects are recorded for this student this term. Say that nothing is recorded yet — not that the student is failing or has no marks.
{% endif %}
{% elif outcome == "subject" %}
SUBJECT_DETAIL for {{ student_label }} — {{ subject_label }}{% if subject_percentage is not none %} ({{ subject_percentage }}%{% if subject_letter %}, {{ subject_letter }}{% endif %}){% endif %}:
{% for item in assignments %}
- {{ item.get('title') or item.get('assignment_id') }}: {% if item.get('status') == "graded" %}{{ item.get('score') }}/{{ item.get('max_score') }}{% elif item.get('status') == "excused" %}excused — exempted by the school, not counted{% elif item.get('status') == "missing" %}not submitted — counts as zero{% elif item.get('status') == "submitted_ungraded" %}submitted, not marked yet{% else %}not due yet{% endif %}

{% endfor %}

Explain the subject total using these items when the parent asks why it is what it is. Excused work is excluded from the calculation entirely; work marked not submitted is included as a zero. Do not recompute the total yourself.
{% elif outcome == "attendance" %}
ATTENDANCE for {{ student_label }}{% if term_label %} — {{ term_label }}{% endif %}: present {{ data.get('present_count', 0) }}, absent {{ data.get('absent_count', 0) }}, late {{ data.get('late_count', 0) }}, excused {{ data.get('excused_count', 0) }}, out of {{ data.get('total_sessions', 0) }} sessions{% if data.get('attendance_rate') is not none %} ({{ data.get('attendance_rate') }}%){% endif %}.

Excused absences are authorised by the school and are counted as attended in that percentage. If the parent asks how many days were missed, distinguish unexcused absences from excused ones rather than adding them together.
{% elif outcome == "timetable" %}
{# Three answers, and the two empty ones mean different things. The tool never leaves
   that to be inferred — `status` arrives from the facade — because the plausible
   reading of an empty week is "the child has no lessons", which is false in both cases. #}
{% if status == "no_class" %}
NO_CLASS_THIS_TERM: the school has no class placement on file for {{ student_label }} for this term, so there is no timetable to show. Tell the parent the school has not placed their child in a class for this term yet and that the office can confirm it. Do NOT say the child has no lessons, and do not show a timetable from any other term or child.
{% elif status == "no_timetable" %}
TIMETABLE_NOT_PUBLISHED: {{ student_label }} is in {{ class_label }}, and the school has not published that class's timetable for this term yet. Say exactly that — the timetable is not out yet — and suggest asking the office when it will be. Do NOT say the child has no lessons, and do not invent a schedule.
{% else %}
TIMETABLE for {{ student_label }} — {{ class_label }}{% if term_label %}, {{ term_label }}{% endif %}{% if academic_year_label %} ({{ academic_year_label }}){% endif %}:
{% for day in days %}
{% if day.slots %}
- {{ day.name }}: {% for slot in day.slots %}{{ slot.period_number }}) {% if slot.is_free %}free{% else %}{{ slot.subject }}{% endif %}{% if slot.starts_at %} {{ slot.starts_at }}{% if slot.ends_at %}-{{ slot.ends_at }}{% endif %}{% endif %}{% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %}

{% else %}
- {{ day.name }}: nothing timetabled

{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% if breaks %}

Break periods in the school day: {% for item in breaks %}{{ item.name or "break" }}{% if item.starts_at %} {{ item.starts_at }}{% if item.ends_at %}-{{ item.ends_at }}{% endif %}{% endif %}{% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %}.
{% endif %}

The days above are in the school's own week order — report them in that order and do not reorder them into a week starting on Monday. The numbers are period numbers, not times; state a time only where one is given above, because a school sets its period times separately and some have not fixed them yet.

A day shown as "nothing timetabled" means the school has planned no lesson on that day — it does not mean the child is off school, so do not tell a parent their child has a day off. "Free" is a period the class deliberately has off within a normal school day. Do not add up lessons into a total or invent a subject for an empty slot. No teacher is named in a timetable — if the parent asks who takes a lesson, say you can look that up separately rather than guessing from this.
{% endif %}
{% elif outcome == "class" %}
{% if status == "no_class" %}
NO_CLASS_THIS_TERM: the school has no class placement on file for {{ student_label }} for this term. Tell the parent the school has not placed their child in a class yet and that the office can confirm it. Do not guess a class from anything earlier in the conversation.
{% else %}
CLASS for {{ student_label }}: {{ class_label }}{% if year_label %} ({{ year_label }}){% endif %}.

Give the class exactly as written above — it is the school's own name for it. Do not translate it, renumber it, or convert it into a different format.
{% endif %}
{% elif outcome == "subjects" %}
{% if status == "no_class" %}
NO_CLASS_THIS_TERM: the school has no class placement on file for {{ student_label }} for this term, so there is no subject list to give. Tell the parent the school has not placed their child in a class yet. Do NOT say the child studies no subjects.
{% elif not subjects %}
SUBJECTS_NOT_PUBLISHED: {{ student_label }} is in {{ class_label }}, and the school has not published the subject list for that class this term. Say exactly that and suggest asking the office. Do NOT say the child studies no subjects, and do not list subjects from anywhere else.
{% else %}
SUBJECTS for {{ student_label }}{% if class_label %} — {{ class_label }}{% endif %}: {{ subjects | join("، ") }}.

That is the list as the school records it, in the school's own order. Do not add subjects the parent mentioned, translate the names, or describe it as complete or incomplete — it is what the school has assigned to that class.
{% endif %}
{% elif outcome == "teachers" %}
{% if status == "no_class" %}
NO_CLASS_THIS_TERM: the school has no class placement on file for {{ student_label }} for this term, so there is no teacher list to give. Tell the parent the school has not placed their child in a class yet. Do NOT say the child has no teachers.
{% elif not subject_groups %}
TEACHERS_NOT_ASSIGNED: {{ student_label }} is in {{ class_label }}, and the school has not recorded who teaches that class yet. Say exactly that and suggest asking the office. Do NOT say the child has no teachers, and do not name anyone.
{% else %}
TEACHERS for {{ student_label }}{% if class_label %} — {{ class_label }}{% endif %}:
{% for group in subject_groups %}
- {{ group.subject }}: {{ group.teachers | join("، ") }}

{% endfor %}

Report these names as they stand. Where a subject lists more than one teacher, both teach it — say so rather than picking one. A subject the parent asks about that is not listed above has no teacher recorded for that class; say that instead of guessing. No contact details are given here, so if the parent wants to reach a teacher, direct them to the school office rather than offering a phone number or email.
{% endif %}
{% elif outcome == "subject_teacher" %}
SUBJECT_TEACHER for {{ student_label }} — {{ subject_label }}: {{ teachers | join("، ") }}.

{% if teachers | length > 1 %}
More than one teacher is recorded for this subject in that class, and all of them teach it. Name them all rather than choosing one.
{% endif %}
Report the name exactly as written. No contact details are given here — if the parent wants to reach them, direct them to the school office.
{% endif %}

{# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   ONE RULE, SHARED BY EVERY BRANCH ABOVE, and deliberately outside the chain so that a
   record tool added later inherits it without its author having to know this exists.

   `backend/chat/grounding.py` checks every figure in the answer against THIS text and
   nothing else. A number that is perfectly true but unwritten here — the academic year,
   a total the model added up, a time no period states — reads to that check as invented,
   and on this profile the check is `enforce`: the parent loses the whole answer and is
   told the figures could not be verified. A correct timetable was destroyed exactly that
   way, by the model helpfully naming the school year.

   So the cheapest place to prevent it is here, one sentence, on every record turn.
   ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ #}

Every number you state must appear somewhere above. Do not add the academic year, a total you worked out, a count of lessons or subjects, or a time no period gives — where the figure is not written above, use words instead ("this term", "the first period", "several"). This is not a style preference: a figure that is not in the text above is discarded along with your whole answer.
